<title>POLAND: FIVE MORE POLISH FIRMS SUSPENDED DUE TO FLOODS.</title>
<headline>FIVE MORE POLISH FIRMS SUSPENDED DUE TO FLOODS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Warsaw bourse suspended trade in five firms from Monday due to the threat to them caused by the current flooding in southern Poland, the bourse said in five separate statements.</p>
<p>The statements said main market firms Gorazdze, Olawa, Polifarb Wroclaw and Remak and the parallel market's Viscoplast were being suspended.</p>
<p>They said trade in each company was being suspended &quot;due to...a lack of access to information allowing an appraisal of the influence of the flood on the activity of the firm.&quot;</p>
<p>Late last week the bourse suspended trade in ZEW and Rafako for an indefinite period of time for the same reason.</p>
<p>Water currently covers thousands of square kilometeres of southern Poland and police currently estimate the death toll of the week-old catastrophy at 36.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
